{
 "purpose": "Identify EA's CJK fallback face(s) and their GDI per-glyph integer advances, so lib/ea/fonts/metrics.rb can stop using the fitted CJK_ADVANCE=0.709 for kana/punctuation. Kanji are already solved (dcc911c): advance = logical height, +1 for Carlito bold.",
 "owner": {
  "windows_run": "Peer A Codex",
  "consumer_and_metrics_owner": "Claude ea-bc"
 },
 "constraints": [
  "Report numbers only; do not copy or commit font binaries.",
  "No fitting: we need measured advances per codepoint per face/height/weight."
 ],
 "environment_notes": [
  "Native SVGs were most likely produced on a Japanese-locale Windows; a GitHub windows runner is en-US. Record the runner locale and install Japanese supplemental fonts first: Add-WindowsCapability -Online -Name 'Language.Fonts.Jpan~~~und-JPAN~0.0.1.0'.",
  "Record HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\FontLink\\SystemLink values for Calibri, Cambria, Carlito, Segoe UI, Tahoma, MS Shell Dlg, and HKLM\\...\\FontSubstitutes entries for Carlito/Calibri/Cambria.",
  "Carlito is not a Windows font; install the OFL Carlito (google/fonts ofl/carlito) on the runner for one pass, and also measure with face name 'Calibri' (EA writes the SVG family name but may have drawn with Calibri)."
 ],
 "faces_to_measure": [
  "Yu Gothic UI",
  "Yu Gothic",
  "Meiryo UI",
  "Meiryo",
  "MS UI Gothic",
  "MS PGothic",
  "MS Gothic",
  "Calibri",
  "Cambria",
  "Carlito"
 ],
 "logical_heights_px": [
  10,
  12,
  13,
  14,
  17
 ],
 "weights": [
  400,
  700
 ],
 "italic": [
  false,
  true
 ],
 "gdi_calls": [
  "CreateFontW(lfHeight = -H, lfWeight, lfItalic, lfCharSet = DEFAULT_CHARSET, lfQuality = DEFAULT_QUALITY, lfFaceName = face); SelectObject into a screen-compatible DC at 96 DPI (MM_TEXT).",
  "After selecting: GetTextFaceW (actual face), GetTextMetricsW (tmHeight, tmAscent, tmDescent, tmAveCharWidth, tmWeight, tmPitchAndFamily), and whether the face has a real bold (compare tmWeight / GetOutlineTextMetrics otmfsSelection).",
  "Per codepoint: GetCharWidth32W and GetCharABCWidthsW (integer advance). Mark if the glyph is missing in the selected face (GetGlyphIndicesW with GGI_MARK_NONEXISTING_GLYPHS).",
  "Per full target string: GetTextExtentPoint32W on the base face (e.g. Carlito/Calibri/Cambria) — this exercises GDI font linking; compare with the sum of per-glyph advances from each candidate fallback face.",
  "Also DrawTextW(DT_CALCRECT|DT_SINGLELINE|DT_NOPREFIX) width for each full string on the base face, in case EA's measurement goes through DrawText."
 ],
 "advances_vs_extents": "EA's published textLength equals the SUM of per-glyph integer advances at logical height H (metrics.rb, 97-100% exact on 10k Carlito texts), so per-glyph integer advances are the primary need; full-string extents on the base face are the check that font linking picks the same face.",
 "known_native_facts": {
  "kanji": "10 px at H10 regular (Cambria context), 14 at H13 bold (Carlito context), 17 at H17 bold (Cambria context 凡例)",
  "kana_groups": {
   "モデル@H13 bold Carlito": 35,
   "リスク@H13 bold Carlito": 30,
   "モデル@H10 regular Cambria": 22
  },
  "single_glyphs_H10_regular_Cambria": {
   "そ": 7,
   "の": 8,
   "・": 5
  },
  "fullwidth_parens": {
   "（ or ） @H10 regular Cambria": 5,
   "@H13 bold Carlito": 8
  }
 },
